4. **`elif number % 3 == 0:`**: If the first condition is false, it checks if the number is divisible by 3. If true, it prints "Fizz".
5. **`elif number % 5 == 0:`**: If the previous conditions are false, it checks if the number is divisible by 5. If true, it prints "Buzz".
6. **`else:`**: If none of the above conditions are met (the number is not divisible by 3 or 5), it prints the number itself.
